            <div xml:id="d491">

                <pb facs="0732" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1947v05/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/10–747: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-10-07">October 7,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> A–1491. Chauvel asked me today for luncheon with General Juin who is here on a
                    brief trip from Morocco. They both reiterated that the French Government intends
                    to proceed with democratic reform in Morocco. They both insisted that the main
                    obstacle in the way of these reforms is the Sultan of Morocco who objects at
                    every step to anything approaching democratic reform. They both agreed that a
                    time limit must be set for the establishing of self-government in that
                    country.</p>
                <p>General Juin plans to return to Morocco within eight days.</p>
                <closer>[<signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi>
                    </signed>]</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
